# Branch, commit and authorship conventions

Follow this repository’s history (`git log`), not generic defaults.
Branch flow is described in `docs/BRANCHING.md`.

## Branch names

`feature/<short-description>` - lowercase, hyphens, **English**. Hotfixes are
`hotfix/<description>` branched from `main`.

```
feature/invoice-list-filters
feature/client-search
feature/docker-compose
```

## Commits - user as sole author

**Author and committer must be the repository owner only - never Cursor or
another agent.** Do not set `--author` to Cursor, and do not add `Co-Authored-By`
footers for an agent, Cursor, or AI model. Commits must look like the user’s
own work in Git history.

Do not change global `git config`. Use the user’s existing local identity.

## Subject and body format

Subject and body are **English**. No `feat:` / `fix:` / `docs:` prefixes.

After a blank line, one prose paragraph: what changed and **why**, not a bullet list.

```
Add monthly filtering on the invoice list

The dashboard showed every invoice at once and made monthly review hard.
The API and Angular view now filter by period so the portfolio demo shows a
realistic ledger workflow.
```

## Merge commits

`Merge feature/<name>: <description>`, and when the merge carries a release -
include the version in parentheses. Merging `develop` → `main` is
`Merge develop: <summary of the whole package>`.

```
Merge feature/invoice-list-filters: status and date filters
Merge develop: backend API, Angular UI and Docker Compose
```
